---

<ArticleLayout
    title={title}
    description={description}
    author={author}
    authorUrl={authorUrl}
    pubDate={pubDate}
    readingTime={readingTime}
    image={image}
    imageAlt={imageAlt}
    category="SaaS"
    categorySlug="saas"
    headings={headings}
>
  <!-- Introduction -->
  <h2 id="introduction">Know Where Your Time Goes</h2>
  <p>
    As a freelancer, time is literally money. Every hour you work but don't track is potential revenue lost. Every
    project you underestimate erodes your effective hourly rate. Every administrative task that bleeds into billable
    time reduces your earnings.
  </p>
  <p>
    Time tracking isn't just about billing clients accurately—though that's essential. It's about understanding your
    business. Which clients are profitable? Which project types eat more time than expected? How much non-billable work
    are you actually doing? Without data, you're guessing.
  </p>
  <p>
    We tested 12 time tracking apps over three months, focusing on what freelancers actually need: easy capture,
    accurate reporting, seamless invoicing, and minimal friction. We tracked real client work, tested integrations, and
    evaluated both manual and automatic tracking approaches.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Quick answer:</strong> <a href="#toggl">Toggl Track</a> is our top pick for most freelancers—it's fast,
    beautiful, and strikes the perfect balance between features and simplicity. <a href="#harvest">Harvest</a> is best
    if seamless invoicing is critical. <a href="#clockify">Clockify</a> is the best free option with unlimited tracking.
  </p>

  <!-- Quick Picks -->
  <h2 id="quick-picks">Our Top 3 Time Trackers</h2>
  <p>Short on time? Here are our top recommendations for freelancers:</p>
  <ComparisonTable
      columns={quickPicksColumns}
      rows={quickPicksRows}
      caption="Top 3 time tracking apps for freelancers"
  />
  <p>
    All three offer free tiers or trials, so you can test extensively before committing. Keep reading for detailed
    reviews of all 7 apps we recommend.
  </p>

  <!-- Why Freelancers Need Time Tracking -->
  <h2 id="why-time-tracking">Why Freelancers Need Time Tracking</h2>
  <p>
    Time tracking delivers value beyond simple billing:
  </p>

  <h3>Accurate Client Billing</h3>
  <p>
    The most obvious benefit: bill clients for actual hours worked. Without tracking, you'll either undercharge (losing
    money) or overcharge (losing clients). Manual estimates are notoriously inaccurate—studies show people underestimate
    time spent by 30-50%.
  </p>
  <p>
    Time tracking provides documentation too. When a client questions an invoice, you have detailed records of exactly
    what you worked on and when. This professionalism builds trust and prevents disputes.
  </p>

  <h3>Project Profitability Analysis</h3>
  <p>
    Fixed-price projects require accurate time estimates. Track time on every project—even fixed-price ones—to
    understand actual versus estimated hours. This data improves future estimates and reveals unprofitable project
    types.
  </p>
  <p>
    You might discover that certain clients consistently take more time than others, or that specific project phases
    always run over. This intelligence helps you price better and choose better projects.
  </p>

  <h3>Understanding Your True Hourly Rate</h3>
  <p>
    Your billable rate isn't your true hourly rate. Admin work, marketing, invoicing, client communication—all this
    non-billable time reduces your effective rate. If you charge $100/hour but spend half your time on non-billable
    work, your true rate is $50/hour.
  </p>
  <p>
    Tracking all time—billable and non-billable—reveals reality. Maybe you need to raise rates. Maybe you need to
    delegate admin work. Maybe certain clients require too much unpaid communication. You can't optimize what you don't
    measure.
  </p>

  <h3>Productivity Patterns</h3>
  <p>
    Time data reveals when you're most productive. Morning person or night owl? Which days are most focused? When do
    meetings cluster? This self-knowledge helps you schedule deep work during peak hours and protect your most
    productive
    time.
  </p>

  <!-- Detailed Reviews -->
  <h2 id="detailed-reviews">Detailed Time Tracker Reviews</h2>

  <!-- Toggl Track -->
  <h3 id="toggl">1. Toggl Track — Best Overall for Freelancers</h3>
  <p>
    Toggl Track has been the gold standard in time tracking for over a decade, and the latest version is their best yet.
    It combines a beautiful, intuitive interface with powerful features—making it easy enough for beginners but capable
    enough for power users.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes Toggl stand out:</strong> Starting a timer takes one click. The browser extension adds tracking
    buttons directly into tools like Asana, Trello, and GitHub. Reporting is visual and insightful. It's simply pleasant
    to use—which matters when you'll interact with it dozens of times daily.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>One-click tracking:</strong> Start timers instantly from any device or browser</li>
    <li><strong>Browser extension:</strong> Integrates tracking buttons into 100+ web apps</li>
    <li><strong>Project organization:</strong> Clients, projects, tasks, and tags</li>
    <li><strong>Beautiful reports:</strong> Visual dashboards, exportable reports, project summaries</li>
    <li><strong>Pomodoro timer:</strong> Built-in focus timer option</li>
    <li><strong>Idle detection:</strong> Prompts when you forget to stop timer</li>
    <li><strong>Calendar integration:</strong> Import calendar events as time entries</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>For freelancers:</strong> Toggl excels at making tracking effortless. The mobile app is excellent for
    tracking on the go. Reports make invoicing straightforward—export by client and date range. The free tier works well
    for solo freelancers; teams need paid plans.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> Free (up to 5 users, basic features), $10/user/month Starter (billable rates, project
    templates), $20/user/month Premium (scheduling, required fields).
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Drawbacks:</strong> Built-in invoicing requires separate Toggl Invoice subscription. Advanced features like
    billable rates need paid tier. Some users find the project hierarchy (workspace → client → project → task) complex.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/toggl"
      text="Try Toggl Track Free — Our #1 Pick"
      variant="primary"
      program="toggl"
  />

  <!-- Harvest -->
  <h3 id="harvest">2. Harvest — Best for Invoicing Integration</h3>
  <p>
    Harvest is the time tracker built for billing. If turning tracked time into professional invoices is your priority,
    Harvest does it better than anyone. Time flows seamlessly into invoices, which flow into payments. For freelancers
    juggling multiple hourly clients, this integration is transformative.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes Harvest stand out:</strong> The tracking-to-invoice flow is seamless. Track time, mark entries as
    billable, generate invoice, send to client, receive payment—all within Harvest. The invoice templates are
    professional and customizable.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Built-in invoicing:</strong> Generate invoices directly from tracked time</li>
    <li><strong>Payment integration:</strong> Accept credit cards and ACH via Stripe/PayPal</li>
    <li><strong>Expense tracking:</strong> Log expenses alongside time entries</li>
    <li><strong>Budget tracking:</strong> Set project budgets and track against them</li>
    <li><strong>Timesheets:</strong> Approve timesheets for team billing</li>
    <li><strong>Detailed reports:</strong> Team, project, and client analysis</li>
    <li><strong>50+ integrations:</strong> Asana, Trello, Basecamp, QuickBooks, Xero</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>For freelancers:</strong> If you bill hourly clients regularly, Harvest streamlines the entire billing
    cycle.
    Set up client rates, track time, invoice at month-end, and accept payment—one system. The expense tracking is useful
    for reimbursable costs.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> Free (1 seat, 2 projects), $12/user/month Pro (unlimited projects, invoicing,
    integrations).
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Drawbacks:</strong> More expensive than competitors for basic tracking. The free tier's 2-project limit is
    restrictive for most freelancers. Interface feels slightly dated compared to Toggl.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/harvest"
      text="Try Harvest Free — Best for Invoicing"
      variant="primary"
      program="harvest"
  />

  <!-- Clockify -->
  <h3 id="clockify">3. Clockify — Best Free Option</h3>
  <p>
    Clockify offers the most generous free tier in time tracking: unlimited users, unlimited projects, unlimited
    tracking. For freelancers on a budget or those just starting out, Clockify delivers professional time tracking at no
    cost.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes Clockify stand out:</strong> The free tier doesn't feel limited. You get all core features:
    timer, manual entry, projects, reports, and integrations. Paid tiers add team management and advanced features, but
    solo freelancers may never need to upgrade.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Unlimited free tracking:</strong> No limits on time, projects, or users</li>
    <li><strong>Timer and manual entry:</strong> Track in real-time or add entries later</li>
    <li><strong>Project budgets:</strong> Set time or money budgets</li>
    <li><strong>Reports and exports:</strong> Detailed, exportable reports</li>
    <li><strong>Invoicing:</strong> Basic invoicing included in free tier</li>
    <li><strong>80+ integrations:</strong> Browser extension, app integrations</li>
    <li><strong>Kiosk mode:</strong> Shared tablet for team time tracking</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>For freelancers:</strong> Clockify is perfect for getting started with time tracking. No credit card, no
    trial period—just sign up and track. The interface is clean and functional. Reports work well for client billing.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> Free forever (unlimited everything), $4.99/user/month Basic (time audit, targets),
    $6.99/user/month Standard (timesheet approvals), $11.99/user/month Pro (forecasting, expenses).
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Drawbacks:</strong> Less polished than Toggl—more functional than delightful. Mobile app is adequate but not
    exceptional. Advanced reporting requires paid tiers. Invoicing is basic compared to Harvest.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/clockify"
      text="Start Clockify Free — Best Free Option"
      variant="primary"
      program="clockify"
  />

  <!-- Timely -->
  <h3 id="timely">4. Timely — Best Automatic Tracking</h3>
  <p>
    Timely takes a radically different approach: automatic tracking. Install the app, and it runs silently in the
    background, logging every app and website you use. Later, review the timeline and categorize time into projects. No
    forgetting to start timers.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes Timely stand out:</strong> The automatic timeline captures everything—even time you'd forget to
    track manually. AI learns your patterns and suggests project assignments. It's particularly powerful for knowledge
    workers who switch between many apps and contexts.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Automatic tracking:</strong> Background recording of all app/website usage</li>
    <li><strong>AI categorization:</strong> Learns to suggest project assignments</li>
    <li><strong>Memory timeline:</strong> Visual timeline of your entire workday</li>
    <li><strong>Privacy-focused:</strong> Data stays on your device until you approve</li>
    <li><strong>Project management:</strong> Budgets, milestones, team scheduling</li>
    <li><strong>Team features:</strong> Capacity planning, workload balancing</li>
    <li><strong>Integrations:</strong> Calendar, project tools, accounting software</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>For freelancers:</strong> Timely captures time that manual tracking misses—those 10-minute emails, quick
    Slack conversations, research tangents. The weekly review shows a complete picture of where time actually went.
    Great for identifying time leaks.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> 14-day trial, then $11/user/month Starter, $20/user/month Premium, $28/user/month
    Unlimited.
    No free tier.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Drawbacks:</strong> Requires review time to categorize tracked entries. Doesn't capture offline work well.
    More expensive than manual trackers. The automatic approach isn't for everyone—some prefer intentional tracking.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/timely"
      text="Try Timely — Automatic Time Tracking"
      variant="secondary"
      program="timely"
  />

  <!-- RescueTime -->
  <h3 id="rescuetime">5. RescueTime — Best for Productivity Insights</h3>
  <p>
    RescueTime focuses on productivity awareness rather than client billing. It automatically tracks app and website
    usage, categorizes activities as productive or distracting, and provides insights into your work patterns. For
    freelancers wanting to understand and improve how they spend time, it's invaluable.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes RescueTime stand out:</strong> The productivity scoring and categorization is excellent. See at a
    glance how much time went to productive work versus distractions. Set goals, block distracting sites, and track
    focus time trends over weeks and months.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Automatic tracking:</strong> Passive monitoring of all computer activity</li>
    <li><strong>Productivity scoring:</strong> Categorize apps as productive, neutral, or distracting</li>
    <li><strong>Focus sessions:</strong> Block distracting sites during work time</li>
    <li><strong>Goals and alerts:</strong> Set targets and receive notifications</li>
    <li><strong>Trends and reports:</strong> Long-term productivity analysis</li>
    <li><strong>Integrations:</strong> Calendar, Slack, project management tools</li>
    <li><strong>Offline time:</strong> Manual entry for meetings and offline work</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>For freelancers:</strong> Use RescueTime alongside a billing-focused tracker. It answers questions like:
    "How much time do I actually spend on deep work?" "What are my biggest distractions?" "Am I more productive mornings
    or afternoons?" This self-awareness drives improvement.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> Free (limited features, 3-month data), $12/month Premium (full features, unlimited data).
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Drawbacks:</strong> Not designed for client billing—no project hierarchy or invoicing. Requires computer
    usage (doesn't track phone time in free tier). The categorization sometimes needs manual adjustment. Privacy
    concerns
    for some users.
  </p>
  <AffiliateButton
      href="/go/rescuetime"
      text="Try RescueTime — Productivity Insights"
      variant="secondary"
      program="rescuetime"
  />

  <!-- Paymo -->
  <h3 id="paymo">6. Paymo — Best Time + Project Management Combo</h3>
  <p>
    Paymo combines time tracking with full project management—tasks, milestones, Gantt charts, file sharing, and team
    collaboration. For freelancers who want one tool for managing projects and tracking time, Paymo eliminates the need
    for separate apps.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes Paymo stand out:</strong> The integration between project management and time tracking is
    seamless. Create tasks, track time against them, and invoice for completed work—all in one interface. Gantt charts
    and kanban boards help manage complex projects.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Full project management:</strong> Tasks, subtasks, milestones, dependencies</li>
    <li><strong>Multiple views:</strong> List, board, Gantt chart, calendar</li>
    <li><strong>Time tracking:</strong> Timer or manual entry on tasks</li>
    <li><strong>Invoicing:</strong> Create invoices from tracked time</li>
    <li><strong>Expense tracking:</strong> Log project expenses</li>
    <li><strong>File management:</strong> Attach files to projects and tasks</li>
    <li><strong>Client access:</strong> Share project progress with clients</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>For freelancers:</strong> Paymo works well for freelancers managing multiple projects with various tasks and
    deliverables. Track time at the task level, see project progress visually, and bill accurately. The all-in-one
    approach reduces tool switching.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> Free (1 user, limited features), $5.95/user/month Starter (time tracking, invoicing),
    $10.95/user/month Small Office (resource scheduling, Gantt).
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Drawbacks:</strong> Jack of all trades—project management isn't as deep as dedicated tools. Interface is
    busy with many features. Mobile app is functional but not great. Fewer integrations than specialized trackers.
  </p>
