      text="Try Paymo — Time + Project Management"
      variant="secondary"
      program="paymo"
  />

  <!-- Hours -->
  <h3 id="hours">7. Hours — Best for Apple Users</h3>
  <p>
    Hours is a beautifully designed time tracker built exclusively for Apple devices. If you work entirely within the
    Apple ecosystem and value design elegance, Hours offers the most polished iOS and Mac experience available.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>What makes Hours stand out:</strong> The visual timeline shows your entire day at a glance—swipe to adjust
    entry times, tap to add notes. The design follows Apple's human interface guidelines, feeling native in a way
    cross-platform apps can't match.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Key features:</strong>
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Visual timeline:</strong> See and edit your day graphically</li>
    <li><strong>Apple Watch app:</strong> Track from your wrist</li>
    <li><strong>Siri integration:</strong> Start timers with voice commands</li>
    <li><strong>Widget support:</strong> iOS home screen widgets</li>
    <li><strong>iCloud sync:</strong> Seamless sync across Apple devices</li>
    <li><strong>Focus mode:</strong> Respect iOS Focus settings</li>
    <li><strong>Export options:</strong> CSV, PDF for invoicing</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <strong>For freelancers:</strong> Hours suits Apple-only freelancers who appreciate beautiful design. The timeline
    view is unique and intuitive. Apple Watch tracking is convenient for quick time capture. Best for personal tracking;
    limited team or invoicing features.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Pricing:</strong> $7.99/month Personal, $11.99/month Pro (team features, advanced exports). No free tier but
    offers trial.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Drawbacks:</strong> Apple-only—no Windows, Android, or web version. Limited integrations compared to
    cross-platform apps. Invoicing is basic (export only). Team features are minimal.
  </p>
