  <!-- How to Choose -->
  <h2 id="how-to-choose">How to Choose the Right Time Tracker</h2>
  <p>
    With several excellent options, here's how to pick the right time tracker for your freelance business:
  </p>

  <h3>By Primary Need</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Best overall:</strong> Toggl Track</li>
    <li><strong>Best for invoicing:</strong> Harvest</li>
    <li><strong>Best free option:</strong> Clockify</li>
    <li><strong>Best automatic tracking:</strong> Timely</li>
    <li><strong>Best productivity insights:</strong> RescueTime</li>
    <li><strong>Best with project management:</strong> Paymo</li>
    <li><strong>Best for Apple users:</strong> Hours</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>By Business Type</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Hourly consultants:</strong> Harvest (tracking → invoice → payment flow)</li>
    <li><strong>Project-based freelancers:</strong> Toggl or Paymo (project tracking, estimates)</li>
    <li><strong>Creative professionals:</strong> Timely (capture context-switching time)</li>
    <li><strong>Solopreneurs on budget:</strong> Clockify (free unlimited tracking)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>By Budget</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Free:</strong> Clockify (unlimited), Toggl Free (5 users), RescueTime Free</li>
    <li><strong>Under $10/month:</strong> Toggl Starter ($10), Hours ($8), Paymo Starter ($6)</li>
    <li><strong>$10-15/month:</strong> Harvest Pro ($12), Timely Starter ($11), RescueTime Premium ($12)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Key Features to Consider</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Tracking method:</strong> Manual timer, automatic, or both?</li>
    <li><strong>Invoicing needs:</strong> Built-in or integration with existing tool?</li>
    <li><strong>Platform coverage:</strong> What devices do you work from?</li>
    <li><strong>Integrations:</strong> Does it connect to your project management and accounting tools?</li>
    <li><strong>Reporting depth:</strong> What insights do you need?</li>
    <li><strong>Team vs. solo:</strong> Will you need to add team members?</li>
  </ol>

